Look up palettes for 4-bit and 8-bit texels of every format

On the N64, while other_mode_h's TEXTLUT field turns palettes on (gDPSetTextureLUT with G_TT_RGBA16 or G_TT_IA16), the
RDP reads every 4-bit and 8-bit texel as an index into the palette that G_LOADTLUT copied into TMEM, whatever format
the tile gives: a texel tagged IA or I is then an index, just like a CI one. Fast3D used the palette only for tiles in
the CI format, and decoded the others as intensity and alpha, so such a picture came out in grey levels, with the
wrong pixels transparent. WCW/nWo Revenge draws its 2D pictures this way: func_8009EC58 loads a picture's palette of
16 or 256 entries and turns palettes on, then func_80096D8C and func_80096A6C load the texels as IA4 or IA8 tiles and
draw them with texture rectangles.

ImportTexture now treats a 4-bit or 8-bit tile of any format as CI while palettes are on: it is decoded
through the palette by ImportTextureCi4 or ImportTextureCi8, in the palette type that patch 0005 reads, and its
texture cache entry is a CI one, keyed by the palette too. Turning palettes on or off changes TEXTLUT, which patch 0005
already makes Fast3D notice, so the next triangle or rectangle imports the texture again.

Not in LibUltraShip main on 2026-11-08; drop this patch once it is there.

diff --git a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
index ce68004a..e65c56ea 100644
